        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ resta nel suo feed: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ stops the whole export. Files already written stay." : {
      "comment" : "The last sentence of the alert an export shows when a chapter nests too deeply. %@ is the name of the Cancel Export button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ detiene toda la exportación. Los archivos ya escritos se conservan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ through the book" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the reader's percent button. %@ is the percent, such as 22.9%.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ del libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ times speed" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver and braille say for the playback speed of an audiobook, such as \"1.25 times speed\". %@ is the speed's number, such as 1.25.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Velocidad %@ veces"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ to %@" : {
      "comment" : "A range of three or more consecutive pages of a PDF, in a list of pages. %1$@ is the first page and %2$@ the last, identifiers written without digit grouping.\nPart of a spoken audio export's file name: a range of the book. %1$@ is where it begins and %2$@ where it ends, each a heading's words or the beginning or end of the book, as in \"Chapter 1 to Chapter 3\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ to %2$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ a %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ to convert its Ogg audio to AAC. Free some space, and TextMouth converts it at the next launch." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert about one book's Ogg audio that waits for disk space. %@ is what the book needs, such as \"“Harbor Dramas” needs 4.2 GB free\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ para convertir su audio Ogg a AAC. Libera espacio y TextMouth lo convertirá la próxima vez que se abra."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ per convertire il suo audio Ogg in AAC. Libera dello spazio e TextMouth lo convertirà al prossimo avvio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ to convert their Ogg audio to AAC. Free some space, and TextMouth converts them at the next launch." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert about several books' Ogg audio that waits for disk space. %@ is what each book needs, listed as a sentence lists them, such as \"“A” needs 1 GB free and “B” needs 2 GB free\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ para convertir su audio Ogg a AAC. Libera espacio y TextMouth lo convertirá la próxima vez que se abra."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ per convertire il loro audio Ogg in AAC. Libera dello spazio e TextMouth lo convertirà al prossimo avvio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ total remaining at current speed" : {
      "comment" : "Part of the time bar's spoken label: the time left for the listed books at the reading speed now set. %@ is a spoken time, such as 3 hours 20 minutes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ restantes en total a la velocidad actual"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ tries again, %@ quits without saving, %@ keeps TextMouth open." : {
      "comment" : "Last line of the alert's message, saying what each button does. %1$@ is the name of the first button, which tries saving again, %2$@ the name of the second, which quits without saving, and %3$@ the name of the third, which keeps TextMouth open. Keep each name exactly as the buttons show it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ tries again, %2$@ quits without saving, %3$@ keeps TextMouth open."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ vuelve a intentarlo, %2$@ sale sin guardar, %3$@ mantiene TextMouth abierto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ twice" : {
      "comment" : "A keyboard shortcut that is its key pressed twice quickly, as spoken or shown. %@ is the shortcut, such as \"W\" or \"Command + I\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ dos veces"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ use plain http, so others can read or change what they send; TextMouth still loads it." : {
      "comment" : "What the Import OPML sheet says of several new feeds whose addresses use plain http, which is not encrypted. %@ is a list of their titles.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ usan http simple, así que otras personas pueden leer o cambiar lo que envían; TextMouth los carga de todos modos."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ usano http semplice, quindi altri possono leggere o modificare ciò che inviano; TextMouth li carica comunque."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ uses it in the menus" : {
      "comment" : "The reason, said after \"not recorded\", why a key cannot be a shortcut: a command of the Mac's own menus uses it. %@ is that command's name, such as Quit TextMouth or Copy. Lower case in English, since it follows a colon.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ lo usa en los menús"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ uses plain http, so others can read or change what it sends; TextMouth still loads it." : {
      "comment" : "What the Import OPML sheet says of one new feed whose address uses plain http, which is not encrypted. %@ is the feed's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ usa http simple, así que otras personas pueden leer o cambiar lo que envía; TextMouth lo carga de todos modos."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ usa http semplice, quindi altri possono leggere o modificare ciò che invia; TextMouth lo carica comunque."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ waits for a network without data limits to refresh by itself." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed's automatic refresh did not run now: the network has data limits. %@ is the feed's title or server.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ espera una red sin límites de datos para actualizarse por sí solo."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ attende una rete senza limiti di dati per aggiornarsi da solo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was connected, so recordings use it." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the Record window when a microphone connects and recordings now use it. %@ is the microphone's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ se conectó, así que las grabaciones lo usan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was connected; choose it in the %@ pop-up to record from it." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the Record window when one microphone connects and is added to the Microphone pop-up. %1$@ is the microphone's name and %2$@ is the pop-up's label.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ was connected; choose it in the %2$@ pop-up to record from it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ se conectó; elígelo en el menú emergente %2$@ para grabar con él."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was disconnected, so recording stopped. What was recorded is kept." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when the microphone was unplugged while recording. %@ is the microphone's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ se desconectó, así que la grabación se detuvo. Lo grabado se conserva."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was disconnected, so recordings use %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the Record window when the chosen microphone is unplugged and another takes its place. %1$@ is the microphone that went away and %2$@ is the one recordings use now.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "%1$@ was disconnected, so recordings use %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%1$@ se desconectó, así que las grabaciones usan %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was disconnected. Connect a microphone to record." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the Record window when the chosen microphone is unplugged and no other is connected. %@ is the microphone's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ se desconectó. Conecta un micrófono para grabar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ was not added back: no copy of the text its package held could be kept first, so TextMouth left the text as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Message when adding a book back to the library stopped because no backup of the text it held could be made. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ no se volvió a agregar a la biblioteca: antes no se pudo conservar una copia del texto que tenía su paquete, así que TextMouth dejó el texto como estaba."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ wasn't asked for again, because the drive hasn't answered an earlier read" : {
      "comment" : "Why a file could not be read, in Use This Library's account. %@ names the file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se volvió a pedir %@ porque la unidad no ha respondido a una lectura anterior"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ wasn't downloaded" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement that Download Now could not bring one book to this Mac. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "%@ no se descargó"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "%@ wasn't read within %lld seconds" : {
      "comment" : "Why a file could not be read, in Use This Library's account. %1$@ names the file and %2$lld is how many seconds TextMouth waited, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
