      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Oculta los controles para saltar a un porcentaje"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hides jump to time controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the reader's time button while the jump to time panel is open.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Oculta los controles para saltar a un tiempo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hides this notice without saving anything." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the VoiceOver hint of the failure banner's Dismiss button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Oculta este aviso sin guardar nada."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hold Shift while skipping to use a secondary skip amount." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Shift+Skip pop-ups in the Playback settings. Shift is the key's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mantén pulsada la tecla Mayúsculas al saltar para usar una cantidad de salto secundaria."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Home" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Home\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Inicio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hours between refreshes while TextMouth runs, from 1 to 168" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the refresh interval's number field and stepper. The range is the limits of the number, in hours.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Horas entre actualizaciones mientras TextMouth está abierto, de 1 a 168"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ore tra un aggiornamento e l’altro mentre TextMouth è in esecuzione, da 1 a 168."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How a BRF or BRL file writes each braille cell. Most files use North American Braille ASCII." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the braille file characters pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings. BRF and BRL are braille file formats, and North American Braille ASCII is the name of a braille character code.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cómo escribe un archivo BRF o BRL cada celda braille. La mayoría de los archivos usa North American Braille ASCII."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How fast the voice speaks in the file. It starts at the book's speed." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Speed slider in the Export dialog's spoken audio options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Con qué rapidez habla la voz en el archivo. Empieza con la velocidad del libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How high the voice sounds in the file. It starts at the book's pitch." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Pitch slider in the Export dialog's spoken audio options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Qué tan aguda suena la voz en el archivo. Empieza con el tono del libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How long media commands are blocked after a Bluetooth device disconnects. Raise it if playback resumes after removing headphones." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Bluetooth disconnect delay slider in the Miscellaneous settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuánto tiempo se bloquean las órdenes multimedia después de que se desconecta un dispositivo Bluetooth. Auméntalo si la reproducción se reanuda al quitarte los audífonos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How many braille cells each line holds, from 18 to 80." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Cells per line stepper in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuántas celdas braille tiene cada línea, de 18 a 80."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How many lines each braille page holds, from 4 to 50." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Lines per page stepper in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuántas líneas tiene cada página braille, de 4 a 50."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How many of the newest" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the number field and stepper that say how many of a feed's newest items are listed or downloaded.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuántos de los más recientes"
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quanti dei più recenti"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How soon a second press must follow the first. A key with different single and double press actions waits this long before its single press acts." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the double press time stepper in Settings: what the time is, and that a key that has one action for a single press and another for a double press waits for that time before acting on a single press.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuánto puede tardar la segunda pulsación tras la primera. Una tecla con acciones distintas para la pulsación simple y la doble espera este tiempo antes de ejecutar la simple."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How the BRF writes each braille cell. Most braille displays and embossers read North American Braille ASCII; those set up for German read Eurobraille. To share with a reader elsewhere, export a PEF." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the braille file characters pop-up in the Export dialog's braille options. BRF and PEF are braille file formats, and North American Braille ASCII and Eurobraille are names of braille character codes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cómo escribe el BRF cada celda braille. La mayoría de las líneas braille y de las impresoras braille leen North American Braille ASCII; las configuradas para alemán leen Eurobraille. Para compartir con un lector en otro lugar, exporta un PEF."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How the voice reads a symbol written several times in a row" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the pop-up button that chooses how the voice reads a run of one symbol.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cómo lee la voz un símbolo escrito varias veces seguidas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
