    "Identifier" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows a book's identifier, a code that names it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Identificador"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Identifier: %@" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's identifier row. %@ is the book's identifier code.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Identificador: %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If %@ arrives from %@ later, %@ may keep two copies of it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before opening the library without its index file. %1$@ is the index file's name, which stays as written; %2$@ and %3$@ are the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "If %1$@ arrives from %2$@ later, %3$@ may keep two copies of it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si %1$@ llega más tarde desde %2$@, puede que %3$@ conserve dos copias."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If it is gone, choose %@." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why the library can't open, pointing to the button that opens it anyway. %@ is that button's name, without its ellipsis. \"It\" is the missing file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si ya no está, elige %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If the file arrives from %@ later, it names the same library." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before restoring the library's identity file. %@ is the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si el archivo llega más tarde desde %@, nombra la misma biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If the file is not written in %@, TextMouth refuses it, and nothing changes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What the alert says first of a choice to or from Unicode braille patterns, which the re-read checks byte by byte before it changes anything (BrailleBookReader.requireReadable(_:as:)), so a wrong one is refused at its first line (review of October 30, finding 5): a file not written in the code named codeName, the one chosen, is refused, and nothing changes. \"If the file is not written in Unicode braille patterns, TextMouth refuses it, and nothing changes.\". Placeholders in order: codeName.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si el archivo no está escrito en %@, TextMouth lo rechaza y no cambia nada."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "If the library's own %@ arrives from %@ later, %@ may keep two copies of it, and this Mac and the other would disagree about which library this is." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before giving the library a new identity file. %1$@ is the identity file's name, which stays as written; %2$@ and %3$@ are the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "If the library's own %1$@ arrives from %2$@ later, %3$@ may keep two copies of it, and this Mac and the other would disagree about which library this is."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si el %1$@ de la propia biblioteca llega más tarde desde %2$@, puede que %3$@ conserve dos copias, y esta Mac y la otra no coincidirían en cuál es esta biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ignored When Typing" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Leading Articles pop-up: a title's leading article does not count when typing a title's first letters, but the list keeps its order.",
      "localizations" : {
