    "Its %@ are kept for when you download it again." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says after Delete Download deleted a download whose package kept parts of the listener's. %@ is a list of what is kept, such as \"place and bookmarks\". The verb agrees with a list of several parts.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Para cuando la descargues de nuevo, se conservan: %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its %@ are kept." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence that says what is kept of one deleted download. %@ is a list of what is kept, such as \"place and bookmarks\". The verb agrees with a list of several parts.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Se conservan: %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its %@ is kept for when you download it again." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says after Delete Download deleted a download whose package kept one part of the listener's. %@ is what is kept, such as \"place\" or \"transcript\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Para cuando la descargues de nuevo, se conserva: %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its %@ is kept." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence that says what is kept of one deleted download. %@ is one part that is kept, such as \"place\" or \"transcript\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Se conserva: %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its %lld chapter markers couldn't be written into the file, so it has none." : {
      "comment" : "Said after a save or an export whose audio was written but whose chapter markers could not be. %lld is the number of chapter markers.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Its chapter marker couldn't be written into the file, so it has none."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Its %lld chapter markers couldn't be written into the file, so it has none."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "No se pudieron escribir sus %lld de marcas de capítulo en el archivo, así que no tiene ninguna."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "No se pudo escribir su marca de capítulo en el archivo, así que no tiene ninguna."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "No se pudieron escribir sus %lld marcas de capítulo en el archivo, así que no tiene ninguna."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its book information file, bookInfo.json, could not be saved." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a book could not move into the current library format. bookInfo.json is a file name and stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo guardar su archivo de información del libro, bookInfo.json."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its cleanup is replaced too." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the question asked before a transcript from a file replaces the book's, when the user had cleaned it up.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su limpieza también se reemplaza."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its conditions and sort are deleted. The books, episodes, articles, and feeds it lists stay in the library, and a Library window showing it shows another view." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the question says Delete does, and what it keeps.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Se eliminan sus condiciones y su orden. Los libros, episodios, artículos y canales que muestra permanecen en la biblioteca, y una ventana de la biblioteca que la muestre pasa a mostrar otra vista."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its contents aren't on this Mac yet, so TextMouth hasn't looked inside it." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the report of a conflicting copy: the copy's file is only in the cloud, so TextMouth did not download it to look inside. \"It\" is the copy.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su contenido aún no está en esta Mac, así que TextMouth no ha mirado dentro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its download can't be removed until it has uploaded." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Remove Download was refused after a failed upload.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su descarga no se puede quitar hasta que se haya subido."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its earlier text was kept as %@, in the book's package." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying where a backup of a book's earlier text was kept. %@ is a file name such as content.md.edited-20261024T123012Z, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su texto anterior se conservó como %@, en el paquete del libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its file is now “%@”, since TextMouth can't write its old format." : {
      "comment" : "Said as a save ends and the book's file got a new name because TextMouth can't write the old format. %@ is the file's new name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su archivo ahora se llama “%@”, porque TextMouth no puede escribir su formato anterior."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its folder “%@” goes too when nothing else is in it." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed: the feed's library folder is deleted too when it holds nothing else. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su carpeta “%@” también se elimina cuando no hay nada más en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its folder “%@” is empty, but could not be deleted." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement after Delete Feed: the feed's library folder is empty but could not be deleted. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su carpeta “%@” está vacía, pero no se pudo eliminar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its folder “%@” is gone too." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement after Delete Feed: the feed's library folder was deleted too. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su carpeta “%@” también se eliminó."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its folder “%@” stays, as something else is in it." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the announcement after Delete Feed: the feed's library folder stays because it holds other things. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su carpeta “%@” se queda, porque hay otras cosas en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its headings are real headings, and the contents list links them." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the accessibility summary written into an exported EPUB: the book has headings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Sus encabezados son encabezados reales, y la lista de contenido los enlaza."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its name, conditions, sort, and limit go back to TextMouth's own. Its place in the list and when it is offered stay as they are." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the question says Restore Default does, and what it keeps.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su nombre, condiciones, orden y límite vuelven a los de TextMouth. Su lugar en la lista y cuándo se ofrece permanecen como están."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its only page is %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of that message for a book of one page. %@ is that page's label, an identifier written without digit grouping.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su única página es %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its original file could not be removed, so it was kept at %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of a warning about a book that moved into the current library format. %@ is the path of the original file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo quitar su archivo original, así que se conservó en %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its original file was not changed." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the alert about one book that could not move into the current library format.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Su archivo original no se modificó."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its package name was taken by other content, and no unused name could be found." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book could not move into the current library format. \"Its\" is the book's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Otro contenido ocupó el nombre de su paquete, y no se encontró ningún nombre sin usar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Its pages run from %@ to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of that message. %1$@ is the first page's label and %2$@ the last page's label, identifiers such as i or 300 written without digit grouping.",
      "localizations" : {
