          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't safely read this SSML file, because it defines entities of its own." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an SSML (Speech Synthesis Markup Language) file was refused: it defines XML entities of its own, which could make it far larger when read.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer de forma segura este archivo SSML, porque define entidades propias."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't safely read this SSML file, because it is written in the %@ encoding." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an SSML (Speech Synthesis Markup Language) file was refused: it is in a text encoding TextMouth cannot see through. %@ is the encoding's name as the file declares it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede leer de forma segura este archivo SSML, porque está escrito en la codificación %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't use the braille table chosen in Settings, “%@”, so this export starts from %@." : {
      "comment" : "Shown in the Export dialog's braille options when the table chosen in Settings can't be used. %1$@ is that table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the table the export starts from, in words such as \"Unified English Braille, uncontracted\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't use the braille table chosen in Settings, “%1$@”, so this export starts from %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede usar la tabla de braille elegida en Ajustes, «%1$@», así que esta exportación empieza con %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't use this Mac's table “%@”: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announced when one of this Mac's braille tables, just chosen, was refused by its check. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, a clause.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't use this Mac's table “%1$@”: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede usar la tabla «%1$@» de esta Mac: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth cannot open copy-protected files." : {
      "comment" : "Advice after the refusal of audio that is locked to a store's own player, such as Audible's .aa and .aax files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no puede abrir archivos con protección contra copia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth closed while opening %@, so it wasn't reopened." : {
      "comment" : "Announced at launch after the app closed while it was opening a book. %@ is the book's title, which is not opened again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se cerró al abrir %@, así que no se volvió a abrir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not check this Mac's braille table “%@”: %@. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation was refused: one of this Mac's braille tables could not be checked. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, which stays English.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth could not check this Mac's braille table “%1$@”: %2$@. Try again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo comprobar la tabla de braille «%1$@» de esta Mac: %2$@. Inténtalo de nuevo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not check this Mac's table “%@”: %@. Choose it again to retry." : {
      "comment" : "Announced when one of this Mac's braille tables, just chosen, could not be checked. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, a clause.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth could not check this Mac's table “%1$@”: %2$@. Choose it again to retry."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo comprobar la tabla «%1$@» de esta Mac: %2$@. Elígela de nuevo para reintentar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not check whether to move it to the Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book's original was kept: TextMouth could not read the choice about the Trash. \"It\" is the original file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo comprobar si debía moverlo a la Papelera."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not keep the new copy of “%@”. Choose Cancel to discard the copy, then import the file again." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when Keep Both could not take the waiting mark off the new copy. %@ is the new copy's title. \"Cancel\" is the sheet's Cancel button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo conservar la copia nueva de “%@”. Elige Cancelar para descartar la copia y luego importa el archivo otra vez."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not make a folder to check it in" : {
      "comment" : "Why the check of a braille table of this Mac could not be made, ending a sentence.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo crear una carpeta para comprobarla"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not move %@ to the current library format." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the alert about books that could not move into the current library format. %@ is a count of books, such as \"3 books\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo pasar %@ al formato actual de la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read its library index, the file that records your folders, sort settings, and the order of your books." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the library index recovery sheet: what the unreadable file holds.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo leer el índice de su biblioteca, el archivo que guarda tus carpetas, los ajustes de orden y el orden de tus libros."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the cue sheet “%@”, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a cue sheet of an imported folder or archive was not used, because it could not be read. %@ is the cue sheet's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo leer el archivo CUE “%@”, así que no se usaron sus encabezados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the label file “%@”, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that an Audacity label file of an imported folder or archive was not used, because it could not be read. %@ is the label file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo leer el archivo de etiquetas “%@”, así que no se usaron sus encabezados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list in the previous index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the outcome of saving a rebuilt library index: the reading list could not be kept from the old index.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo leer la lista de lectura del índice anterior."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list in the unreadable index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the library index recovery sheet: the reading list could not be read from the unreadable index.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no pudo leer la lista de lectura del índice ilegible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list or the sort settings in the previous index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the outcome of saving a rebuilt library index: neither the reading list nor the sort settings could be kept from the old index.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
