    "TextMouth is getting them now, and the library opens when they arrive." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why the library can't be used yet: the files are being fetched from the cloud, and the library opens by itself when they arrive. \"Them\" means the library's files named in the sentence before.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los está obteniendo ahora, y la biblioteca se abre cuando lleguen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: books are being moved between folders.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está moviendo libros entre carpetas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is moving books between folders. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está moviendo libros entre carpetas. Espera a que termine y vuelve a elegir %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is not downloading right now." : {
      "comment" : "Why the download of a feed's next episode did not start: the app is quitting or the feed is being deleted. Said after \"The next episode could not be downloaded, so playback stopped.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no está descargando en este momento."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay unsaved in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save stays unsaved: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the changes that could not be saved.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está abriendo de nuevo con otra biblioteca, así que siguen sin guardarse en esta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay where they are in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files stays undone: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está abriendo de nuevo con otra biblioteca, así que siguen donde están en esta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is quitting and the book's audio doesn't hold these edits yet. Discard undoes them; next time you edit this book, Redo brings them back until you make another edit. Cancel keeps TextMouth open." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the question about the audio editor's unsaved edits asked as TextMouth quits: what Discard and Cancel do.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se está cerrando y el audio del libro aún no contiene estas ediciones. Descartar las deshace; la próxima vez que edites este libro, Rehacer las recupera hasta que hagas otra edición. Cancelar mantiene TextMouth abierto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading the library's text again. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why a book can't be read again while the library's text is being read again (the launch batch, Redo Text Extraction), in the words TextMouth uses while its storage work is held (StorageBusyError).",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer el texto de la biblioteca. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again in another encoding. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again in another encoding, in the same words as extractionRefusal: a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otra codificación. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with another braille code. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with another braille code, as the other re-reads' sentences say it (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:), BrailleFileCodeWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otro código braille. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with other braille file characters. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with other braille file characters, as the encoding's sentence says it for any other book (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)): a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está volviendo a leer “%@” con otros caracteres de archivo braille. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: the library is being rebuilt.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reconstruyendo su directorio de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory, the folder that holds the library. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reconstruyendo su directorio de datos. Espera a que termine y vuelve a elegir %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is replacing “%@” with the new copy. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Why an action on a book is refused while Replace Existing makes the new copy ready, such as Edit Text or opening the book. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está reemplazando “%@” por la copia nueva. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still carrying out your last answer. Wait until it finishes." : {
      "comment" : "What an import question says when it is answered again while the previous answer is still being carried out.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sigue procesando tu última respuesta. Espera a que termine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still saving them." : {
      "comment" : "The reason that ends \"Changes to the feed “Planet Money” could not be saved:\" in the quit prompt and banner. Them are the feed's changes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth todavía los está guardando."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth sigue usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is switching to another library and opening again on it." : {
      "comment" : "Why an operation was refused: TextMouth is switching to another library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth está cambiando a otra biblioteca y se abrirá de nuevo con ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to make changes in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen location can't be used: macOS does not let TextMouth write there. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para hacer cambios en %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to post notifications. Turn them on in System Settings, Notifications, TextMouth." : {
      "comment" : "What the notifications setting's help says while macOS does not allow TextMouth to post notifications. System Settings and Notifications are macOS's own names, in the language of macOS.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para enviar notificaciones. Actívalas en Ajustes del Sistema, Notificaciones, TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to use the microphone. Turn it on in System Settings, Privacy & Security, Microphone." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when macOS has denied TextMouth the microphone. Names the places in System Settings, as macOS words them, where the user can allow it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no tiene permiso para usar el micrófono. Actívalo en Ajustes del Sistema, Privacidad y seguridad, Micrófono."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth keeps the original file of audio it converts at import. An original takes about as much disk space as its converted file, or twice as much when uncompressed. Export offers it as the Original file. A feed episode's original is not kept: it can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Keep Originals switch while it is on. \"Original file\" names the choice Export offers; keep it the same as that choice's translation.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth conserva el archivo original del audio que convierte al importar. Un original ocupa casi tanto espacio en disco como su archivo convertido, o el doble si no está comprimido. Exportar lo ofrece como Archivo original. El original de un episodio de un canal no se conserva: se puede descargar de nuevo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth kept the text you changed in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the message when an automatic rebuild left a book's edited text alone. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth conservó el texto que cambiaste en %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left it there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when one item appeared: TextMouth left the item and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.\nSecond sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth left what was put there and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth lo dejó allí y sigue usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which hold no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that hold no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.spx” and “b.spx”\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que no contienen sonido que pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which holds no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that holds no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que no contiene sonido que pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which need TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.avi” and “b.wmv”\". Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que necesitan el conversor de TextMouth, que falta en la app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which needs TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes. Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth omitió %@, que necesita el conversor de TextMouth, que falta en la app."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth left them there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when several items appeared: TextMouth left the items and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los dejó allí y sigue usando %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth makes a folder named after the feed in %@, and its episodes and articles download into it." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the folder picker of the Add Feed sheet. %@ is the library folder chosen, or the name of the library's top level.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth crea en %@ una carpeta con el nombre del canal, y sus episodios y artículos se descargan en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth makes a new library index from the books in this folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before opening the library without its index file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth crea un índice nuevo de la biblioteca con los libros de esta carpeta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with a problem:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about one book that moved into the current library format with a problem. %@ is a count of books, such as \"1 book\". The book's line follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth pasó %@ al formato actual de la biblioteca, pero con un problema:"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with problems:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about several books that moved into the current library format with problems. %@ is a count of books, such as \"3 books\". The books' lines follow.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth pasó %@ al formato actual de la biblioteca, pero con problemas:"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of four or more duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %lld is the number of books. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copy of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld de copias nuevas de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld copia nueva de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth movió %lld copias nuevas de libros duplicados a la Papelera, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copies of %@ to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of two or three duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %@ is their titles in curly quotes, listed as a sentence lists them. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth movió a la Papelera las copias nuevas de %@, porque no se respondieron las preguntas sobre si conservarlos como duplicados antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlos, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copy of “%@” to the Trash, because the question whether to keep it as a duplicate was never answered before TextMouth closed. To get it back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copy of one duplicate book to the Trash, because its question was never answered. %@ is the book's title. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth movió a la Papelera la copia nueva de “%@”, porque no se respondió la pregunta sobre si conservarlo como duplicado antes de que TextMouth se cerrara. Para recuperarlo, abre la Papelera y elige Volver a colocar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once it has finished moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when books have been moved between folders. \"Them\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los devuelve cuando termine de mover libros entre carpetas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once it has finished rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when the data directory has been rebuilt. \"Them\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los devuelve cuando termine de reconstruir su directorio de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once the move of its data directory ends." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when the move of the data directory ends. \"Them\" is the files.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los devuelve cuando termine el traslado de su directorio de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth needs the drive “%@” connected to open the library." : {
      "comment" : "What using a library on another drive means. %@ is the drive's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth necesita que la unidad «%@» esté conectada para abrir la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth opens the book's manifest.json in your text editor." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the Edit Manifest explanation. manifest.json is a file name and stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth abre el manifest.json del libro en tu editor de texto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth opens the book's text in your text editor, as a Markdown file." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the Edit Text explanation. Markdown is the name of a text format.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth abre el texto del libro en tu editor de texto, como archivo Markdown."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth quit on %@: its memory grew to %@ GB while %@ played, because of a fault in macOS's audio. Your place was saved." : {
      "comment" : "Alert text at the next launch after TextMouth quit to protect the Mac, when a book played. %1$@ is the date and time of the quit; %2$@ is how large its memory grew, in gigabytes, such as 6.1; %3$@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth quit on %1$@: its memory grew to %2$@ GB while %3$@ played, because of a fault in macOS's audio. Your place was saved."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se cerró el %1$@: su memoria creció hasta %2$@ GB mientras se reproducía %3$@, por un fallo del audio de macOS. Se guardó tu posición."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth quit on %@: its memory grew to %@ GB while a book played, because of a fault in macOS's audio. Your place was saved." : {
      "comment" : "Alert text at the next launch after TextMouth quit to protect the Mac, when a book played whose title was not kept. %1$@ is the date and time of the quit; %2$@ is how large its memory grew, in gigabytes, such as 6.1.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth quit on %1$@: its memory grew to %2$@ GB while a book played, because of a fault in macOS's audio. Your place was saved."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se cerró el %1$@: su memoria creció hasta %2$@ GB mientras se reproducía un libro, por un fallo del audio de macOS. Se guardó tu posición."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth quit on %@: its memory grew to %@ GB while nothing was playing. Your place was saved." : {
      "comment" : "Alert text at the next launch after TextMouth quit to protect the Mac, when nothing was playing. %1$@ is the date and time of the quit; %2$@ is how large its memory grew, in gigabytes, such as 6.1.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth quit on %1$@: its memory grew to %2$@ GB while nothing was playing. Your place was saved."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth se cerró el %1$@: su memoria creció hasta %2$@ GB mientras no se reproducía nada. Se guardó tu posición."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth reads BRF and BRL files you add from now on with these characters, and recognizes Unicode braille patterns by itself. The Export dialog starts a BRF with them. A book keeps its import characters, which Book Information can change." : {
      "comment" : "The caption under the braille file characters pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings. BRF and BRL are braille file formats, and Book Information is a window.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "A partir de ahora, TextMouth lee los archivos BRF y BRL que agregues con estos caracteres, y reconoce por sí mismo los patrones braille Unicode. El diálogo Exportar empieza un BRF con ellos. Un libro conserva sus caracteres de importación, que Información del libro puede cambiar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth reads braille files (BRF, BRL, and PEF) with this code and exports with it unless the Export dialog chooses another. A book keeps the code it was imported with." : {
      "comment" : "The caption under the code pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings. BRF, BRL, and PEF are braille file formats.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth lee los archivos braille (BRF, BRL y PEF) con este código y exporta con él, salvo que el diálogo Exportar elija otro. Un libro conserva el código con el que se importó."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth reads its file as it reads a file you add: in the encoding the file names, or else the one TextMouth finds." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What Automatic does, as the alert says it before it is chosen.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth lee su archivo como lee un archivo que agregas: con la codificación que indica el archivo o, si no, con la que TextMouth encuentra."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once it has finished moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when books have been moved between folders. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los guarda cuando termine de mover libros entre carpetas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once it has finished rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when the data directory has been rebuilt. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los guarda cuando termine de reconstruir su directorio de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once the move of its data directory ends." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when the move of the data directory ends. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth los guarda cuando termine el traslado de su directorio de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth skipped %lld entries of “%@”: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after a playlist imported with entries left out. %1$lld is the number of entries skipped, %2$@ the playlist's name, and %3$@ the list of the entries, each with its reason in parentheses.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth skipped %lld entry of “%@”: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth skipped %lld entries of “%@”: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth omitió %lld de entradas de “%@”: %@."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth omitió %lld entrada de “%@”: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth omitió %lld entradas de “%@”: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stopped %@ because %@, and won't try again until TextMouth is closed and opened again." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a library call inside the iPhone app ran too long and was abandoned. %1$@ is the work's name, such as \"the braille translation\" (English until its area converts); %2$@ is why it was stopped, such as \"it ran longer than 11 seconds\" (English until the watchdog's area converts). Read after an import's own words.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth stopped %1$@ because %2$@, and won't try again until TextMouth is closed and opened again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth detuvo %1$@ porque %2$@, y no volverá a intentarlo hasta que cierres y vuelvas a abrir TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stopped %@ earlier because it took too long, and won't try again until TextMouth is closed and opened again." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a library call inside the iPhone app is refused because an earlier one was abandoned for taking too long. %@ is the work's name, such as \"the braille translation\" (English until its area converts). Read after an import's own words.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth detuvo antes %@ porque tardaba demasiado, y no volverá a intentarlo hasta que cierres y vuelvas a abrir TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stopped reading this document because %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a document was refused at import: the program that reads it ran too long or used too much memory and was stopped. %@ is the reason, a clause in English that follows \"because\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth dejó de leer este documento porque %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stopped the braille translation because %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation ended. %@ is the reason, a clause such as \"an earlier call was abandoned\", which stays English until the engine's sentences convert.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth detuvo la traducción a braille porque %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new articles." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of articles.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth deja de revisar este canal en busca de artículos nuevos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new episodes." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of episodes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth deja de revisar este canal en busca de episodios nuevos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new items." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of episodes and articles.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth deja de revisar este canal en busca de elementos nuevos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth waited for it." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why the library can't open: TextMouth waited for the missing file to arrive. \"It\" is the file named in the sentence before.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth lo esperó."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will open the library in %@ instead of the one in %@, which isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before using another library while the one in use is not available. %1$@ is the chosen folder's path; %2$@ is the path of the library in use.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will open the library in %1$@ instead of the one in %2$@, which isn't available."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth abrirá la biblioteca de %1$@ en lugar de la de %2$@, que no está disponible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will open the library in %@ the next time it opens, but it couldn't open again by itself: %@" : {
      "comment" : "First part of the message when Use This Library could not open TextMouth again. %1$@ is the library's folder; %2$@ is the system's reason, a sentence.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will open the library in %1$@ the next time it opens, but it couldn't open again by itself: %2$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth abrirá la biblioteca de %1$@ la próxima vez que se abra, pero no pudo abrirse de nuevo por sí mismo: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will quit and open again to load it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before using another library: TextMouth opens again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth saldrá y se abrirá de nuevo para cargarla."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will quit and open again to start it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before starting a new library: TextMouth opens again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth saldrá y se abrirá de nuevo para iniciarla."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will start a new, empty library in the default location, %@, instead of the library in %@, which isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before starting a new library. %1$@ is the default location's path; %2$@ is the path of the library in use, which is not available.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will start a new, empty library in the default location, %1$@, instead of the library in %2$@, which isn't available."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth iniciará una biblioteca nueva y vacía en la ubicación predeterminada, %1$@, en lugar de la biblioteca de %2$@, que no está disponible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will stop using the library in %@ (%@) and open the library in %@ instead." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before using another library. %1$@ is the path of the library in use; %2$@ is what it holds, such as \"743 books, 2 feeds\"; %3$@ is the chosen folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will stop using the library in %1$@ (%2$@) and open the library in %3$@ instead."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth dejará de usar la biblioteca de %1$@ (%2$@) y abrirá la biblioteca de %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth writes %@ with a new identity for the library, and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before giving the library a new identity file. %@ is the identity file's name, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth escribe %@ con una identidad nueva para la biblioteca y la abre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth writes %@ with the identity this Mac knows for the library, and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before restoring the library's identity file. %@ is the identity file's name, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth escribe %@ con la identidad que esta Mac conoce de la biblioteca y la abre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's converter could not make itself safe before reading “%@”, so it did not read the file." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter could not confine itself before reading it, so it did not read the file. %@ is the file's name. Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El conversor de TextMouth no pudo protegerse antes de leer “%@”, así que no leyó el archivo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's converter gave back audio of “%@” that TextMouth could not read." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: what TextMouth's converter gave back was not audio TextMouth reads, which only a damaged copy of the app could make. %@ is the file's name. Advice to install the app again follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El conversor de TextMouth devolvió audio de “%@” que TextMouth no pudo leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's converter stopped before the end of “%@”, so it could not be imported." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter ended before the end of its sound, with no error. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El conversor de TextMouth se detuvo antes del final de “%@”, así que no se pudo importar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's converter stopped unexpectedly while reading “%@”. The file may be damaged." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter stopped unexpectedly while reading it, as a damaged file can make it do. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El conversor de TextMouth se detuvo inesperadamente al leer “%@”. Puede que el archivo esté dañado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%@”. They are %@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of a filter TextMouth doesn't run itself. %1$@ is the filter's name as typed, and %2$@ the list of the filters TextMouth does run, such as \"a, b, and c\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%1$@”. They are %2$@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los filtros propios de TextMouth no incluyen “%1$@”. Son %2$@; con ffmpeg instalado, funciona cualquier filtro que tenga."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters run this chain." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under a filter preset's chain field: every filter in it is one TextMouth runs itself.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los filtros propios de TextMouth ejecutan esta cadena."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own loudnorm normalizes with one gain, so it takes only true" : {
      "comment" : "What the loudnorm filter's linear option accepts, said at the end of a refusal such as \"The loudnorm filter's linear can't be “false”: <this>.\" Written without its full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "el loudnorm de TextMouth normaliza con una sola ganancia, así que solo acepta true"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own rules are newer, version %@. To use them, delete your copy or copy their rules into it." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the rules that come with the app are newer than the user's copy. %@ is the new version number, written without digit grouping.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Las reglas propias de TextMouth son más recientes, versión %@. Para usarlas, elimina tu copia o copia sus reglas en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth: no build details recorded" : {
      "comment" : "A line of the speech refusal report: the app recorded nothing about how it was built.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth: no se registraron detalles de la compilación"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That OPML file is damaged at line %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: its markup is damaged. The first %@ is the line number of the fault, an identifier written without digit grouping. The second is a short technical reason in English, from the parser, kept English as detail for a bug report.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "That OPML file is damaged at line %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ese archivo OPML está dañado en la línea %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That OPML file lists no feeds." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it lists no feed TextMouth can subscribe to.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ese archivo OPML no incluye canales."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That address isn't a web address TextMouth can open." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed could not be fetched: its address is not an http or https address.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Esa dirección no es una dirección web que TextMouth pueda abrir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That file is empty." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it is empty.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ese archivo está vacío."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That file isn't an OPML list of subscriptions." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it is another kind of file.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ese archivo no es una lista OPML de suscripciones."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That isn't a web address. Enter a feed's address, or the address of a page that names one." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the address typed is not a web address.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Eso no es una dirección web. Escribe la dirección de un canal, o la de una página que nombre uno."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That item isn't a plain file TextMouth can read." : {
      "comment" : "Alert explaining why a chosen item was not attached as a transcript: it is not an ordinary file, such as a folder or a pipe.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Ese elemento no es un archivo normal que TextMouth pueda leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That keeps the book's copy in the cloud." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Remove Download was refused: what the service's own command does.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Eso mantiene la copia del libro en la nube."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That match is no longer in the book's text. Search again to find it." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when a search match is no longer in the book's text.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Esa coincidencia ya no está en el texto del libro. Busca de nuevo para encontrarla."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That page doesn't name a feed." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the web page names no feed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Esa página no nombra ningún canal."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That page names %lld feeds. Choose one, then Subscribe." : {
      "comment" : "What the Add Feed sheet says when a web page names several feeds. %lld is how many feeds the page names. Subscribe is the name of the Subscribe button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "That page names %lld feed. Choose one, then Subscribe."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "That page names %lld feeds. Choose one, then Subscribe."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Esa página nombra %lld de canales. Elige uno y luego Suscribirse."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Esa página nombra %lld canal. Elige uno y luego Suscribirse."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Esa página nombra %lld canales. Elige uno y luego Suscribirse."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That would put %@ %lld levels deep, but folders nest at most %lld levels." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a folder edit would nest a folder too deep. %1$@ is the folder's location, in straight double quotes. %2$lld is how many levels deep it would be. %3$lld is the most levels allowed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "That would put %@ %lld level deep, but folders nest at most %lld levels."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
