        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo escribir el audio convertido de %1$@ (%2$@)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio converted from %@ failed its check: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a converted audio file was refused: it failed the check made after conversion. %1$@ is the source file's name and %2$@ the reason, a phrase with no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The audio converted from %1$@ failed its check: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio convertido de %1$@ no superó su comprobación: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio couldn't be exported." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor's export fails. A sentence giving the reason follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo exportar el audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio file that the edits need can't be read as audio.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer el audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio editor" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Works in pop-up of a keyboard shortcut: the shortcut works only in the audio editor's windows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El editor de audio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio editor for %@ is already open." : {
      "comment" : "Said when Edit Audio… is chosen for a book whose editor is already open; that window comes forward. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El editor de audio de %@ ya está abierto."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ could not be read for converting." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: it could not be read as audio, or it is only in the cloud. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer el archivo de audio %@ para convertirlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ ends before its audio does, so it could not be converted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: the file stops before the audio its header promises. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ termina antes que su audio, así que no se pudo convertir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ has %lld channels but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file was not converted: it has more than two channels and does not say which is which, so a mix to stereo would keep two arbitrary channels. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$lld the number of channels, always more than two.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The audio file %@ has %lld channel but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The audio file %@ has %lld channels but does not say which is which, so TextMouth cannot mix it to stereo."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld de canales pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld canal pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ tiene %lld canales pero no indica cuál es cuál, así que TextMouth no puede mezclarlo a estéreo."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ is damaged, so it could not be converted." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: a checksum failed or a field holds a value no encoder writes. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ está dañado, así que no se pudo convertir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file %@ is not the kind of file its name says." : {
      "comment" : "Why an audio file could not be converted at import: its bytes are not of the format its extension names. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de audio %@ no es del tipo que indica su nombre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio file “%@” that the edits need is missing from the book." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio file that the edits need is missing. %@ is its path inside the book's package.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Falta en el libro el archivo de audio “%@” que necesitan las ediciones."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio is only in the cloud, not on this Mac yet." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio file that the edits need is only in the cloud. A second sentence says to download the book and try again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio solo está en la nube, todavía no en esta Mac."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio isn't ready to play yet." : {
      "comment" : "Said when Play is pressed in the audio editor before the edited audio is ready, or after it couldn't be made ready.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio aún no está listo para reproducirse."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio of %@ couldn't be opened for editing." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor couldn't open a book. %@ is the book's title. A sentence giving the reason follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo abrir el audio de %@ para editarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audio of “%@” is being edited. Close the audio editor or wait for it to save, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: the library's copy has its audio open in the audio editor. %1$@ is the book's title. %2$@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The audio of “%1$@” is being edited. Close the audio editor or wait for it to save, then choose %2$@ again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio de “%1$@” se está editando. Cierra el editor de audio o espera a que se guarde, y vuelve a elegir %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audiobook's audio, your place, and your bookmarks stay as they are." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the question asked before an audiobook's transcript is deleted or replaced by a file's: what stays.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El audio del audiolibro, tu posición y tus marcadores se quedan como están."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The audiobook's title in your library." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint and tooltip of the Title field in the Record window.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El título del audiolibro en tu biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The book" : {
      "comment" : "How an announcement names a book whose title is not known, as in \"The book can't move up.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The book %@ is stored at %@, outside the data directory, so the move cannot carry it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory was refused. %1$@ is the book's title; %2$@ is the path where its file is stored.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The book %1$@ is stored at %2$@, outside the data directory, so the move cannot carry it."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El libro %1$@ está guardado en %2$@, fuera del directorio de datos, así que el traslado no puede llevarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The book can be transcribed again." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before an audiobook's transcript is deleted, after what stays.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El libro se puede volver a transcribir."
          }
