    },
    "The braille code for reading and writing braille." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the braille code pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El código braille para leer y escribir braille."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The braille code the book is written in." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the braille code pop-up in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El código braille en el que está escrito el libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The braille is translated to print again with this code. Nothing checks that it is the right choice. If words read wrongly, choose another." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What the alert says first: the braille is translated to print again with the code chosen, and nothing can tell whether it is the right one, since every braille text translates in every table, so a wrong one reads with no error.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El braille se vuelve a traducir a texto impreso con este código. Nada comprueba que sea la elección correcta. Si las palabras se leen mal, elige otro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The braille table writes an eight-dot cell, %@, but TextMouth's BRF and PEF files are six-dot only." : {
      "comment" : "Why braille could not be written to a BRF or PEF file: the braille table writes an eight-dot cell. %@ names the cell's dots, such as \"dots 4 and 7\". BRF and PEF are braille file formats.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La tabla de braille escribe una celda de ocho puntos, %@, pero los archivos BRF y PEF de TextMouth son solo de seis puntos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The braille table writes “%@” as an eight-dot cell, but TextMouth's BRF and PEF files are six-dot only." : {
      "comment" : "Why braille could not be written to a BRF or PEF file: the braille table writes a character with an eight-dot cell. %@ is the print character. BRF and PEF are braille file formats.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La tabla de braille escribe «%@» como una celda de ocho puntos, pero los archivos BRF y PEF de TextMouth son solo de seis puntos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The chosen table is built into TextMouth (liblouis %@)." : {
      "comment" : "Under the pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings: the chosen braille table comes with TextMouth. %@ is the version of liblouis, the braille library, written as a version number.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La tabla elegida está integrada en TextMouth (liblouis %@)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The chosen table is one of this Mac's VoiceOver braille tables (liblouis %@)." : {
      "comment" : "Under the pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings: the chosen braille table is one of this Mac's. %@ is the version of liblouis, the braille library, written as a version number.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La tabla elegida es una de las tablas de braille de VoiceOver de esta Mac (liblouis %@)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The chosen table is one of this Mac's VoiceOver braille tables." : {
      "comment" : "Under the pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings: the chosen braille table is one of this Mac's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La tabla elegida es una de las tablas de braille de VoiceOver de esta Mac."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The clipboard has no text to paste, so the text is unchanged." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the announcement when Paste from Clipboard finds no text on the clipboard.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El portapapeles no tiene texto que pegar, así que el texto no cambió."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cloud service" : {
      "comment" : "How a sentence names the cloud service when it is unknown, at the start of the sentence, so it has a capital letter.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El servicio en la nube"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The copy just imported is incomplete." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the last paragraph of the question asked about a duplicate book whose new copy is missing chapters. What it lacks follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La copia recién importada está incompleta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The copy made in the library did not match the original, so the copy was discarded." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book could not move into the current library format: the copy differed from the original.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La copia hecha en la biblioteca no coincidía con el original, así que se descartó."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The copy was already complete when Cancel was pressed, so the move went ahead." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence added to the done message of a move of the library when Cancel was pressed after the copy was complete.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La copia ya estaba completa cuando se pulsó Cancelar, así que el traslado siguió adelante."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The correction file %@ is damaged or belongs to another recording, so %@ could not be converted." : {
      "comment" : "Why a hybrid WavPack file could not be converted at import: the correction file beside it (the same name ending in .wvc) is damaged or belongs to another recording. %1$@ is the correction file's name and %2$@ the WavPack file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The correction file %1$@ is damaged or belongs to another recording, so %2$@ could not be converted."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de corrección %1$@ está dañado o pertenece a otra grabación, así que no se pudo convertir %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cue sheet “%@” is too large to read." : {
      "comment" : "Refusal of a cue sheet that is larger than TextMouth reads. %@ is the cue sheet's file name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo CUE “%@” es demasiado grande para leerlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cue sheet “%@” names none of the audio beside it, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a cue sheet of an imported folder or archive was not used, because it names none of the audio beside it. %@ is the cue sheet's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo CUE “%@” no nombra ningún audio junto a él, así que no se usaron sus encabezados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The current data directory does not exist." : {
      "comment" : "Why a move of the data directory was refused: the folder it would move from is missing.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El directorio de datos actual no existe."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The current directory will be retained as recovery data." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before moving the library: the old folder is kept.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El directorio actual se conservará como datos de recuperación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The cursor is %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Go to Page when the cursor is not on the page typed and there is no known reason. %@ says where the cursor is, such as \"on page 52\" or \"before page 1\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El cursor está %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The data directory has no Logs folder, so logs go to %@ until it has one." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings while the data directory has no Logs folder. %@ is the folder's full path, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El directorio de datos no tiene carpeta Logs, así que los registros van a %@ hasta que la tenga."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The data directory is missing, so logs go to %@ until it is back." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings while the data directory is missing. %@ is the folder's full path, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Falta el directorio de datos, así que los registros van a %@ hasta que vuelva."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The data directory's Logs folder can't be written (%@), so logs go to %@ until it can." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings while the data directory's Logs folder cannot be written. %1$@ is the reason the system gives, which may be in English, and %2$@ is the folder's full path, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The data directory's Logs folder can't be written (%1$@), so logs go to %2$@ until it can."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se puede escribir en la carpeta Logs del directorio de datos (%1$@), así que los registros van a %2$@ hasta que se pueda."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The destination folder %@ is no longer in the library." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a move is refused because the folder it goes into is gone from the library. %@ is that folder's location, in straight double quotes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta de destino %@ ya no está en la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The details could not be copied" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when Copy Details could not copy the report of a speech refusal to the pasteboard.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudieron copiar los detalles"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The disk is almost full, so recording stopped. What was recorded is kept." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when the disk filled up while recording.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El disco está casi lleno, así que la grabación se detuvo. Lo grabado se conserva."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The disk is too full to keep this audio for pasting." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the disk is too full to keep the audio cut or copied in the audio editor for Paste.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El disco está demasiado lleno para conservar este audio y pegarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The disk lacks room: this needs about %@, and TextMouth keeps %@ free. Free some space, then export again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a spoken audio export was refused: the disk is too full. %1$@ is the space the export needs and %2$@ the space TextMouth always keeps free, each a size such as 1 GB.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The disk lacks room: this needs about %1$@, and TextMouth keeps %2$@ free. Free some space, then export again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No hay espacio suficiente en el disco: esto necesita unos %1$@, y TextMouth mantiene libres %2$@. Libera espacio y vuelve a exportar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The download of %@ wasn't removed" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement that Remove Download did not remove one book's files. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se quitó la descarga de %@"
          }
