        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo en sí no se ha modificado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "Begins a sentence about a file that could not be read in the text encoding chosen for it, such as \"The file “Ledger.txt” can't be read as Shift JIS (Japanese): …\". %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%@”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” declares the text encoding “%@”, but it holds bytes that are not valid in that encoding." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a file could not be imported: an HTML file declares a text encoding its bytes are not valid in. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the encoding's name as the file spells it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” declares the text encoding “%2$@”, but it holds bytes that are not valid in that encoding."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” declara la codificación de texto “%2$@”, pero contiene bytes que no son válidos en esa codificación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” declares the text encoding “%@”, which TextMouth cannot read." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a file could not be imported: an HTML file declares a text encoding TextMouth does not know. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the encoding's name as the file spells it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” declares the text encoding “%2$@”, which TextMouth cannot read."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” declara la codificación de texto “%2$@”, que TextMouth no puede leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” in this DAISY book refers to “%@”, outside the book's folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a DAISY book kept as loose files could not be imported: one of its files refers to a file outside the book's folder. %1$@ is the referring file's path inside the folder and %2$@ the reference, as the file writes it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” in this DAISY book refers to “%2$@”, outside the book's folder."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” de este libro DAISY hace referencia a “%2$@”, fuera de la carpeta del libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” in this archive is damaged or incomplete: %@. Get a fresh copy of the archive, then import it again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a ZIP archive or comic book archive (a ZIP of pictures named .cbz) could not be imported: a file inside it is damaged. %1$@ is the file's path inside the archive and %2$@ the reason, a phrase in English that begins with a lowercase letter and has no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” in this archive is damaged or incomplete: %2$@. Get a fresh copy of the archive, then import it again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” de este archivo comprimido está dañado o incompleto: %2$@. Consigue una copia nueva del archivo comprimido y vuelve a importarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” in this book is damaged or incomplete: %@. Get a fresh copy of the book, then import it again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book could not be imported (a DAISY book, an EPUB book, or an audiobook): a file inside it is damaged. %1$@ is the file's path inside the book and %2$@ the reason, a phrase in English that begins with a lowercase letter and has no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” in this book is damaged or incomplete: %2$@. Get a fresh copy of the book, then import it again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” de este libro está dañado o incompleto: %2$@. Consigue una copia nueva del libro y vuelve a importarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” in this document is damaged or incomplete: %@. Get a fresh copy of the document, then import it again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a Word or OpenDocument document could not be imported: a file inside it is damaged. %1$@ is the file's path inside the document and %2$@ the reason, a phrase in English that begins with a lowercase letter and has no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” in this document is damaged or incomplete: %2$@. Get a fresh copy of the document, then import it again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” de este documento está dañado o incompleto: %2$@. Consigue una copia nueva del documento y vuelve a importarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file “%@” is damaged or incomplete: it begins with a %@ byte-order mark, but the rest is not valid %@ text." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a file could not be imported: it begins with the byte-order mark of a Unicode encoding, but the bytes after it are not valid in that encoding. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ and %3$@ are both the encoding's standard name, such as UTF-16LE, which stays as it is.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The file “%1$@” is damaged or incomplete: it begins with a %2$@ byte-order mark, but the rest is not valid %3$@ text."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo “%1$@” está dañado o incompleto: empieza con una marca de orden de bytes %2$@, pero el resto no es texto %3$@ válido."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The file's address isn't a web address TextMouth can open." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed item's download failed: its address is not an http or https address.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La dirección del archivo no es una dirección web que TextMouth pueda abrir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The files of the new copy of “%@” are no longer in the library, so it can't be kept. Choose Cancel, then import the file again." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when the new copy's files are gone while the question waited. %@ is the new copy's title. \"Cancel\" is the sheet's Cancel button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los archivos de la copia nueva de “%@” ya no están en la biblioteca, así que no se puede conservar. Elige Cancelar y luego importa el archivo otra vez."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The files that couldn't be read are listed." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the results of Compare Libraries saying the unread files are listed below.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Se enumeran los archivos que no se pudieron leer."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The filter chain is empty." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said when a filter chain is typed as nothing at all, in the audio editor's Apply Filter and the filter presets.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La cadena de filtros está vacía."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The filter presets are reset to the defaults." : {
      "comment" : "Said as every filter preset is put back to TextMouth's premade ones.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los preajustes de filtros volvieron a sus valores predeterminados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder %@ can't be found." : {
      "comment" : "Why the library can't be used: its folder is missing. %@ is the folder's path. For a folder in a cloud service, a sentence about the likely cause follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se encuentra la carpeta %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder %@ holds %lld other items: %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen folder can't be used: it holds other items. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$lld is how many items; %3$@ is their names as a short list.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The folder %@ holds %lld other item: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The folder %@ holds %lld other items: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta %1$@ contiene %2$lld de elementos más: %3$@."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta %1$@ contiene %2$lld elemento más: %3$@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta %1$@ contiene %2$lld elementos más: %3$@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder %@ holds a different library, so nothing was compared." : {
      "comment" : "What the Compare Libraries sheet says when the chosen folder holds a different library. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta %@ contiene una biblioteca distinta, así que no se comparó nada."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder %@ is in %@ and isn't on this Mac yet." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen folder can't be used: it is only in the cloud. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$@ is the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The folder %1$@ is in %2$@ and isn't on this Mac yet."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta %1$@ está en %2$@ y aún no está en esta Mac."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder %@ is in the Trash." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen folder can't be used: it is in the Trash. %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta %@ está en la Papelera."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder already has that name and location." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a folder edit would leave the folder exactly as it is.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta ya tiene ese nombre y esa ubicación."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder chosen for this feed is no longer in the library. Choose another folder." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the folder chosen for the feed was removed from the library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta elegida para este canal ya no está en la biblioteca. Elige otra carpeta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder chosen is no longer in the library. Choose another folder." : {
      "comment" : "Why Move to Library did nothing: the folder chosen was removed from the library. Follows \"Could not move to the library: \".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta elegida ya no está en la biblioteca. Elige otra carpeta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder chosen to hold the feed's folder is no longer in the library. Choose another one." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe could not make the feed's folder: the folder chosen to hold it was removed from the library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta elegida para contener la carpeta del canal ya no está en la biblioteca. Elige otra."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder for this feed is no longer in the library. Choose another folder for it." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed's episode could not be downloaded: the feed's folder was removed from the library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta de este canal ya no está en la biblioteca. Elige otra carpeta para él."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder holds %lld DAISY books (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a folder could not be imported as one DAISY book: its top level holds several books' package files. %lld is how many books, always two or more, and %@ their file names, separated by commas.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The folder holds %lld DAISY book (%@)."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "The folder holds %lld DAISY books (%@)."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta contiene %lld de libros DAISY (%@)."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta contiene %lld libro DAISY (%@)."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "La carpeta contiene %lld libros DAISY (%@)."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder is no longer in the library. It may have been moved, renamed, or deleted in another window." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a folder edit is refused because the folder is gone from the library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta ya no está en la biblioteca. Puede que se haya movido, renombrado o eliminado en otra ventana."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder is not a DAISY book: it has no ncc.html or .opf file at its top level." : {
      "comment" : "Why a folder could not be imported as a DAISY book: it holds no navigation file (ncc.html) and no package file (.opf) at its top level. ncc.html and .opf are file names and stay as they are.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta no es un libro DAISY: no tiene un archivo ncc.html ni .opf en su nivel superior."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder is there, but TextMouth can't read its library identity file: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Why the library can't be used: the file that names the library can't be read. %@ is the reason, a phrase or sentence from the system or TextMouth.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta está ahí, pero TextMouth no puede leer el archivo de identidad de su biblioteca: %@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder is there, but it holds a different TextMouth library." : {
      "comment" : "Why the library can't be used: the folder holds another library than the one this Mac uses.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta está ahí, pero contiene otra biblioteca de TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder is there, but the library isn't in it." : {
      "comment" : "Why the library can't be used: the folder exists but holds no library.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta está ahí, pero la biblioteca no está en ella."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folder of %@ is no longer in the library." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says when a feed's row is opened and its library folder was removed. %@ is the feed's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La carpeta de %@ ya no está en la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The folders %@ and %@ can't both move into %@: their names mean the same folder on this disk." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when two folders moved together would land on the same name. %1$@ and %2$@ are the two folders' names, in straight double quotes. %3$@ is where they go: a folder's location in straight double quotes, or the name of the library's top level.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The folders %1$@ and %2$@ can't both move into %3$@: their names mean the same folder on this disk."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Las carpetas %1$@ y %2$@ no pueden moverse juntas a %3$@: sus nombres significan la misma carpeta en este disco."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The heading whose section ends the audio, with its subheadings, or the end of the book." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the To pop-up in the Export dialog's spoken audio options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El encabezado cuya sección termina el audio, con sus subencabezados, o el final del libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The headings from %@ run past the end of the audio, so the tracks were imported without them." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after an import of tracks that came without the headings of some cue sheets and label files, because a heading lay past the end of the audio. %@ is the files' names in curly quotes, listed as a sentence lists them.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Los encabezados de %@ pasan del final del audio, así que las pistas se importaron sin ellos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The import was stopped before its end." : {
      "comment" : "What the Import OPML sheet says once the listener stopped the import before its end.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La importación se detuvo antes de terminar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The index is not changed until you choose %@ or %@, which stay available from %@ at the top of the library." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of what Continue Reading does. %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of the Try Again and Rebuild Library Index buttons; %3$@ is the name of the Recovery Options button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The index is not changed until you choose %1$@ or %2$@, which stay available from %3$@ at the top of the library."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El índice no cambia hasta que elijas %1$@ o %2$@, que siguen disponibles en %3$@, en la parte superior de la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The label file “%@” matches no audio file beside it by name, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that an Audacity label file of an imported folder or archive was not used, because no audio file beside it has its name. %@ is the label file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El archivo de etiquetas “%@” no coincide por nombre con ningún archivo de audio junto a él, así que no se usaron sus encabezados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The labels of the label file “%@” run past the end of its audio, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that an Audacity label file of an imported folder or archive was not used, because its labels lie past the end of its audio. %@ is the label file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Las etiquetas del archivo de etiquetas “%@” pasan del final de su audio, así que no se usaron sus encabezados."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The language of the braille code for reading and writing braille." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the language pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El idioma del código braille para leer y escribir braille."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The language of the braille code the book is written in." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the language pop-up in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El idioma del código braille en el que está escrito el libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The library already had different content under its package name, %@, so it was stored in a new package, %@, and its original file was kept at %@." : {
      "comment" : "Warning about a book that moved into the current library format. %1$@ is the name of the package that already held other content; %2$@ is the name of the new package; %3$@ is the path where the original file was kept.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The library already had different content under its package name, %1$@, so it was stored in a new package, %2$@, and its original file was kept at %3$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La biblioteca ya tenía contenido distinto con el nombre de paquete %1$@, así que se guardó en un paquete nuevo, %2$@, y su archivo original se conservó en %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The library at %@ isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "Error text when the library's folder can't be used. It follows what failed, as in \"Listening statistics could not be saved: The library at /Volumes/Backup/TextMouth isn't available.\" %@ is the folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La biblioteca de %@ no está disponible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The library can't be reached, so TextMouth can't keep the new copy of “%@”. Answer again once it is back." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when Keep Both or Replace Existing is chosen while the library cannot be reached. %@ is the new copy's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se puede acceder a la biblioteca, así que TextMouth no puede conservar la copia nueva de “%@”. Responde de nuevo cuando vuelva."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The library can't move books now. Try again once it is available." : {
      "comment" : "Why Move to Library did nothing: the library's index is being recovered or the data directory is away or moving. Follows \"Could not move to the library: \".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "La biblioteca no puede mover libros ahora. Inténtalo de nuevo cuando esté disponible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The library can't move while a book is open. Close %@ first." : {
      "comment" : "Why a move of the library was refused: a book is open in a reader. %@ is the book's title, in quotation marks.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
