      }
    },
    "When Applicable" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). A visibility as the Visibility pop-up names it: \"Always\", \"When Applicable\", or \"Hidden\". This is the case .whenApplicable.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando corresponda"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When New Episodes Arrive" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the third group of the Feeds tab of Settings: alerts and notifications. Title case.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando llegan episodios nuevos"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When a book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the Reading List's options bar pop-up button choosing what a book opened from the list does when it ends: play the book below, play the book above, or stop.\nLabel of the pop-up button in a folder's settings choosing what happens when one of its books ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al terminar un libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When a book is deleted, %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the explanation in Storage settings of what removing a book does. %@ says what happens to the book's files, such as \"its files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando se elimina un libro, %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When an article ends" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up button in a news feed's Feed Info choosing what happens when one of its articles ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando termina un artículo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When an episode ends" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up button in a podcast feed's Feed Info choosing what happens when one of its episodes ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando termina un episodio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When an item ends" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up button in a feed's Feed Info choosing what happens when one of its items ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando termina un elemento"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When articles are ignored, a book whose metadata names French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Catalan, Swedish, Danish, or Norwegian passes over that language's articles, such as Le and Die, and The." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the note under the Leading Articles pop-up, shown where articles are ignored. Names the languages whose articles TextMouth skips; Le, Die, and The are example articles and stay as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Cuando se ignoran los artículos, un libro cuyos metadatos indican francés, alemán, español, italiano, portugués, neerlandés, catalán, sueco, danés o noruego omite los artículos de ese idioma, como Le y Die, además de The."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the pop-up in the Playback settings that chooses what happens when a book ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al terminar el libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When checked, matches must use the same upper and lower case" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Match Case checkbox.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está marcada, las coincidencias deben usar las mismas mayúsculas y minúsculas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When checked, the search text is an ICU regular expression" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Regular Expression checkbox in the Search Library window. ICU is the name of the regular expression syntax, and stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está marcada, el texto de búsqueda es una expresión regular ICU"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When checked, this feed follows the setting in Settings, %@; uncheck it to give the feed its own" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the checkbox that makes a feed follow the global setting. %@ is the name of the Feeds tab of Settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, este canal sigue el ajuste de Ajustes, %@; desactívalo para darle uno propio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When enabled, playback starts automatically after jumping to a heading, bookmark, or search result" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Auto-play after navigation checkbox in the Playback settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, la reproducción empieza automáticamente después de saltar a un encabezado, un marcador o un resultado de búsqueda"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When enabled, search text is treated as a regular expression" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Use Regex switch in Search in Book.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, el texto de búsqueda se trata como una expresión regular"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When enabled, use \\b in the pattern for word boundaries" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Regular expression switch in the substitution rule editor. \\b is regular expression syntax and stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, usa \\b en el patrón para los límites de palabra"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When off, its files are deleted permanently and cannot be recovered." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the hint of the setting that moves deleted files to the Trash: what happens with the setting off.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está desactivado, sus archivos se eliminan de forma permanente y no se pueden recuperar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When off, removing a book will %@ at once." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the hint of the setting that confirms before removing a book. %@ is what deleting does, such as \"move the files to the Trash\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está desactivado, quitar un libro implica %@ de inmediato."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When off, the sheet stays open showing the remaining time and a reset button" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Close sheet after setting timer checkbox in the Playback settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está desactivado, la hoja sigue abierta y muestra el tiempo restante y un botón de reinicio"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When on, a braille file read as contracted Unified English Braille that is clearly English Braille, American Edition is read as that instead." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the guess switch in the Braille tab of Settings. Unified English Braille and English Braille, American Edition are the names of braille codes.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, un archivo braille leído como Unified English Braille contraído que sea claramente English Braille, American Edition se lee como este último."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When on, a deleted book's files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of the setting that moves deleted files to the Trash: what happens with the setting on.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, los archivos de un libro eliminado van a la Papelera, donde puedes recuperarlos hasta que se vacíe."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When on, removing a book first asks whether to %@ or keep them in the TextMouth library folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of the setting that confirms before removing a book. %@ is what deleting does, such as \"move the files to the Trash\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si está activado, al quitar un libro se pregunta primero si quieres %@ o conservarlos en la carpeta de la biblioteca de TextMouth."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When resuming playback, rewind to the start of this unit" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Rewind to pop-up in the Playback settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al reanudar la reproducción, retrocede hasta el inicio de esta unidad"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When this book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the book's own settings menu that chooses what happens when this book ends.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al terminar este libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When you save, TextMouth checks the manifest and rearranges the book, keeping your place in its track." : {
      "comment" : "Fourth sentence of the Edit Manifest explanation: what happens when the user saves the manifest.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al guardar, TextMouth comprueba el manifiesto y reorganiza el libro, conservando tu lugar en su pista."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When you save, the book updates and keeps your place as near as it can." : {
      "comment" : "Fourth sentence of the Edit Text explanation: what happens when the user saves the edited text.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al guardar, el libro se actualiza y conserva tu lugar lo mejor que puede."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the lines of a speech refusal report that say where in the book speech stopped.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Dónde"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where Am I (End)" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the event whose sound is chosen in Settings, Sound Effects: the Where Am I announcement ends. Where Am I is the name of a command.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Dónde estoy? (final)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where Am I (Start)" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the event whose sound is chosen in Settings, Sound Effects: the Where Am I announcement starts. Where Am I is the name of a command.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Dónde estoy? (inicio)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where Am I?" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Information group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks a short summary of the reading position. Also the title of the menu command of the same name.\nName of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks the position and the selection.\nTitle of the reader toolbar's button that says where the reader is in the book.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Dónde estoy?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where Am I? Announces current position in the book" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls the reader toolbar's Where Am I? button while nothing is announced.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Dónde estoy? Anuncia la posición actual en el libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where Am I? Full Summary" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Information group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks the full summary of the reading position. Also the title of the menu command of the same name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Dónde estoy? Resumen completo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %@ keeps them with your books, so they move and sync with the library. %@ keeps them in %@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line; existing logs stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint and tooltip of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings. %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of its two choices, as the pop-up lists them, and %3$@ is the folder's path on this Mac, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %1$@ keeps them with your books, so they move and sync with the library. %2$@ keeps them in %3$@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line; existing logs stay."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Dónde escribe TextMouth sus registros de diagnóstico. %1$@ los guarda con tus libros, así que se mueven y se sincronizan con la biblioteca. %2$@ los guarda en %3$@, que nunca se sincroniza. Un cambio se aplica desde la línea siguiente; los registros existentes permanecen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where none of their words are left, %@, each goes to about the same point in its chapter, or to the nearest passage the two readings share." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of what a re-read does to the listener's place and bookmarks. %@ is an example of when that happens, such as \"as when garbled letters become Cyrillic\", set between commas.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Donde no queda ninguna de sus palabras, %@, cada uno va aproximadamente al mismo punto de su capítulo, o al pasaje más cercano que comparten las dos lecturas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where none of their words are left, each goes to about the same point in its chapter, or to the nearest passage the two readings share." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of what a re-read does to the listener's place and bookmarks, without an example.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Donde no queda ninguna de sus palabras, cada uno va aproximadamente al mismo punto de su capítulo, o al pasaje más cercano que comparten las dos lecturas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where the audio begins: the book's beginning, or a heading." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the From pop-up in the Export dialog's spoken audio options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Dónde empieza el audio: el inicio del libro o un encabezado."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whether each page's last line carries its braille page number." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Braille page numbers switch in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si la última línea de cada página lleva su número de página braille."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whether that code's braille is contracted, which writes common words and letter groups in fewer cells." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the contraction pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si el braille de ese código está contraído, lo que escribe palabras y grupos de letras comunes con menos celdas."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whether that code's braille is contracted." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the contraction pop-up in the Export dialog's braille options.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Si el braille de ese código está contraído."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Which track of %@ do you want to edit?" : {
      "comment" : "Question asked before editing a book of several audio tracks. %@ is the book's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "¿Qué pista de %@ quieres editar?"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, %@ was changed to lead to %@ instead of %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: the new location's link was changed while the data was copied. %1$@ is the link's path; %2$@ is where it leads now; %3$@ is where it led before.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %1$@ was changed to lead to %2$@ instead of %3$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mientras TextMouth copiaba sus datos, %1$@ se cambió para llevar a %2$@ en lugar de %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld items appeared in %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: items appeared in the new location while the data was copied. %1$lld is how many; %2$@ is the new location's path; %3$@ is their names as a list.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld item appeared in %@: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld items appeared in %@: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "many" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Mientras TextMouth copiaba sus datos, aparecieron %1$lld de elementos en %2$@: %3$@."
                }
              },
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Mientras TextMouth copiaba sus datos, apareció %1$lld elemento en %2$@: %3$@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "machine_translated",
                  "value" : "Mientras TextMouth copiaba sus datos, aparecieron %1$lld elementos en %2$@: %3$@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, something else was put at %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: something else was put at the new location while the data was copied. %@ is the new location's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mientras TextMouth copiaba sus datos, se puso algo más en %@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While playing, moves Book content on with the speech, even as you read it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of Follow in Braille in iPhone Settings. \"Book content\" is the name of the element that holds the book's text, as VoiceOver reads it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Mientras se reproduce, mueve el contenido del libro junto con la voz, incluso mientras lo lees."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whole File" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the audio editor's Apply Filter sheet: filter all of the audio.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Archivo completo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Whole word only" : {
      "comment" : "A part of a substitution rule's spoken summary: the rule matches whole words only.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Solo palabras completas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
