            "value" : "“%1$@” se convierte en “%2$@”: %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” beside the audio wasn't attached: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Notice after an import: a transcript file found beside the audio was not attached. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ is the reason, a sentence.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” beside the audio wasn't attached: %2$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@” junto al audio no se adjuntó: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” can't be read as %@: %@ Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why the book titled bookTitle was not read again with the braille file characters named codeName: its file is not braille in them, as reason, the reader's own sentence (BrailleFileError), says, and nothing changed. It has the shape of an encoding's refusal (TextEncodingWording.notValidRefusal(bookTitle:encoding:)): \"“Ledger” can't be read as Eurobraille, six-dot (German-speaking countries): Line 3 holds the control character U+0007, which is not Eurobraille. Nothing was changed.\". Placeholders in order: bookTitle, codeName, reason.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” can't be read as %2$@: %3$@ Nothing was changed."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%1$@” no se puede leer como %2$@: %3$@ No se cambió nada."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” changed while it was being replaced, so TextMouth left both copies as they are. Choose Replace Existing again." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when the library's copy changed while the new copy was being made ready. %@ is the book's title. \"Replace Existing\" is a button of the question.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” cambió mientras se reemplazaba, así que TextMouth dejó ambas copias como están. Elige Reemplazar el existente de nuevo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” could not be moved back after a failed move, so its files are at %@ instead of %@: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Failure notice: a book's files could not be put back after a move failed. %1$@ is the book's title; %2$@ is where its files are now; %3$@ is where they belong; %4$@ is the reason, a sentence from the system.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” could not be moved back after a failed move, so its files are at %2$@ instead of %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo devolver «%1$@» a su sitio tras un traslado fallido, así que sus archivos están en %2$@ en lugar de %3$@: %4$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” couldn't be downloaded from iCloud. Check the connection, then add it again." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says when a file's download from iCloud stalled and the import was cancelled. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo descargar «%@» desde iCloud. Comprueba la conexión y vuelve a agregarlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” couldn't be read: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when an audio file cannot be read. %1$@ is the audio file's name; %2$@ is the reason, a short phrase in English.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” couldn't be read: %2$@."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "No se pudo leer “%1$@”: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” downloads once this Mac is on a network without data limits." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed item's download did not run now: the network has data limits. Says the same as the row's wait reason. %@ is the item's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” se descargará cuando esta Mac esté en una red sin límites de datos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” holds no DAISY book and no audio tracks to import as one book." : {
      "comment" : "What the library says as a folder chosen to import holds no DAISY book and no audio tracks. %@ is the folder's name. A sentence about what it holds follows.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” no contiene ningún libro DAISY ni pistas de audio para importar como un solo libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” holds no sound to import." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: it holds no sound, such as a video without a sound track. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” no contiene sonido que importar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” is a Personal Voice, which macOS can't record to a file. Choose another voice with the %@ button in the reader, then export again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a spoken audio export was refused: the book's voice is a Personal Voice. %1$@ is the voice's name and %2$@ the name of the Voice button in the book's reader.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "“%1$@” is a Personal Voice, which macOS can't record to a file. Choose another voice with the %2$@ button in the reader, then export again."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "«%1$@» es una Voz personal, que macOS no puede grabar en un archivo. Elige otra voz con el botón %2$@ del lector y vuelve a exportar."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” is a pronunciation lexicon, not a playlist." : {
      "comment" : "Refusal of a .pls file that is a pronunciation lexicon, not a playlist. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” es un léxico de pronunciación, no una lista de reproducción."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” is already being added to the library." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says when Cancel Download comes too late: the download's book is already being imported. %@ is the title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "“%@” ya se está agregando a la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "“%@” is an XML file, but not a pronunciation lexicon." : {
      "comment" : "Message of the alert when a file chosen as a pronunciation lexicon is XML of another kind. %@ is the file's name.",
      "localizations" : {
